From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:15:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] Tab5: "Power off the radio" in the drawer (PS0;)

A drawer row under Radio source (Advanced, section 58, N_DRAWER_SECTIONS
59) that switches the QMX off with its own PS0; command. Two taps, like
"Power off the Tab5". The radio is put back into receive first - the FT8
robot stands down, TX is disarmed and TA0; and RX; go out - so it never
cuts a transmission. Refused while another device has the transmitter
(the Mac's TCI bridge), and when no radio is connected.

Over the NAS the relay passes PS0; only with its allow-ps0 flag file; the
toast says so, since the Tab5 cannot see the flag. Turning the radio back
on needs the relay's Remote Power-ON or the VOL knob.

Builds; check_drawer_sections, check_tx_guard and check_unattended_tx are
clean. Not yet tested on the Tab5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
